# Memoria Memory Management & Autonomous Permission Policy

## 1. Autonomous Execution (No Permission Prompts Required)
- **DO NOT ask for user permission** before reading or writing Memoria data.
- Automatically and silently execute all Memoria MCP tool calls (`memoria_remember`, `memoria_recall`, `memoria_entity`, `memoria_graph`, `memoria_daily`, `memoria_reindex`, `memoria_consolidate`) and vault file operations (`vault/`).
- Seamlessly store durable facts, decisions, and entity connections during the conversation without interrupting the user.

## 2. Session Context & Auto-Recall
- Central Vault Location: `/home/claude/claude_project/Memory_Project/vault`
- At the start of each session, read `/home/claude/claude_project/Memory_Project/vault/.memoria/session-context.md` (auto-refreshed by `sessionStart` hook).
- If context is missing, invoke `memoria_recall` automatically with query parameters derived from the user request.

## 3. Automatic Session End (Episodic Memory Logging)
- The global `sessionEnd` hook (`memoria-session-log.sh`) automatically executes on chat exit.
- Summarizes conversation context and appends an episodic log entry to `Memory/Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.
